  <dashboards>
    <dashboard name='Glossary'>
      <repository-location derived-from='http://ip-172-31-0-134:8291/t/GlobalStandardReporting/workbooks/MarketingOfflineCompetitionSpendsGranular/Glossary?rev=' id='Glossary' path='/t/GlobalStandardReporting/workbooks/MarketingOfflineCompetitionSpendsGranular' revision='' site='GlobalStandardReporting' />
      <style>
        <style-rule element='dash-text'>
          <format attr='vertical-align' id='dash-text_3' value='top' />
        </style-rule>
      </style>
      <size maxheight='800' maxwidth='1000' minheight='800' minwidth='1000' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='4' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone forceUpdate='true' h='98000' id='3' type-v2='text' w='98400' x='800' y='1000'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri,sans-serif' fontsize='14' underline='true'>Glossary</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri,sans-serif' fontsize='10' underline='true'>Spends:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri,sans-serif' fontsize='10'> Trackable gross spends (eg. some sponsorships or OOH formats might not be available). </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri,sans-serif' fontsize='10' underline='true'>TV GRP:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri,sans-serif' fontsize='10' underline='true'>Æ </run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri,sans-serif' fontsize='10'>Gross Rating Point (Target Rating Point) is a common, traditional TV metric that evaluates advertising impact. It is calculated as a percentage of the total market reached within a specified demographic, multiplied by the exposure frequency.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri,sans-serif' fontsize='10' underline='true'>TV Channel:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri,sans-serif' fontsize='10'> Refers to TV channel where particular ad was aired.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri,sans-serif' fontsize='10' underline='true'>Daypart (TV/Radio):</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri,sans-serif' fontsize='10'> Refers to specific timeframe when ad was aired. Naming unified among countries, but actual daypart might slightly differ on media plans.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri,sans-serif' fontsize='10'>Æ </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri,sans-serif' fontsize='10' underline='true'>Spot Duration (TV/Radio):</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri,sans-serif' fontsize='10'> Length of TV/Radio ad (in seconds).</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri,sans-serif' fontsize='10' underline='true'>Spot Frequency (TV/Radio):</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri,sans-serif' fontsize='10'> Total number of TV/Radio ads on air in selected period.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri,sans-serif' fontsize='10' underline='true'>TV Type:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri,sans-serif' fontsize='10'> Refers to type of broadcasting the signal is transmitted e.g. Terrestrial TV or Cable TV.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri,sans-serif' fontsize='10' underline='true'>OOH:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri,sans-serif' fontsize='10'> Out of home, outdoor advertising.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri,sans-serif' fontsize='10' underline='true'>Media Format:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri,sans-serif' fontsize='10'> Type of out of home advertising with main types: Transit, Street furniture, Billboards, Digital (names vary by country - localised).</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri,sans-serif' fontsize='10' underline='true'>OOH Channel:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri,sans-serif' fontsize='10'> If available, more detailed information on media format eg Transit ( media format) could be further split into LCD in station, Taxi videos, bus wrap etc).</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri,sans-serif' fontsize='10' underline='true'>OOH Media House:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri,sans-serif' fontsize='10'> Vendor owning Out of home placement e.g JCDecaux.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri,sans-serif' fontsize='10'>Æ </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri,sans-serif' fontsize='10' underline='true'>OOH Location:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri,sans-serif' fontsize='10'> If available, city/location of specific placement.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri,sans-serif' fontsize='10' underline='true'>Channel distribution by brand (Top level overview):</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri,sans-serif' fontsize='10'> Refers to media mix split in offline channels (Radio, TV, OOH etc).</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='4' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
      </zones>
